 beyond, the window lights of distant buildings and the warm patches of the wet street lamps on the ground enter the sharp focal plane one after another, the focus shift proceeding evenly and continuously.\nFrom 2.20 s to 5.20 s the camera begins to pull back, the pull-back rate is slow and even, and the frame of the glass gradually expands toward both sides within the frame; at the same time the focus moves slowly back from outside the window, passes through the glass and enters the interior, and the warm desk lamp of the study, the dark wooden desk edge and the wall bookshelf enter the depth of field one after another and sharpen gradually, the camera height stays level, the vertical edges of the interior objects stay vertical, the floor runs along the bottom of the frame and the ceiling along the top.\nFrom 5.20 s to 8.00 s the pull-back rate shifts from slow to fast, the frame opens up at an accelerating pace, and it finally settles into a medium shot of the study: the protagonist sits at the desk with both hands typing continuously on the laptop keyboard, the cold light of the screen falls on the backs of his hands and on the desk top, and the lamp on the right supplies the warm key light; the camera is placed behind and to the side of the protagonist and slightly above shoulder height, showing his back, his shoulder line and the contour of his side profile in the frame, with his line of sight passing over his shoulder to land on the desk top and the screen. The whole pull-back is a single continuous shot, and the glass frame, the scene outside the window and the interior objects stay at the same spatial positions the entire time.\n\noverall_soundscape: The low-frequency airflow of the night wind outside the window and the steady hum of the distant city; the faint sound of the glass vibrating slightly; after the camera enters the interior it turns into close-field sound - the crisp continuous rhythm of keyboard strokes, the fine hum of the desk lamp current, the slight creak of the chair seat as the body's centre of gravity shifts, and the steady low drone of the laptop fan.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A low, gentle synthesizer bed continues from the opening, swelling sustained string notes join in the middle section as the pull-back unfolds, the density of the strings increases as the pull-back accelerates, and it comes to rest on a stable chord over the protagonist's keyboard action, with the final note decaying naturally.","宽度":"1344","高度":"768","视频秒数":"8"}}}],"widgets_values_named":{"data":{"md_path":"D:\\\\Comfy\\\\stories\\\\七纹刻印\\\\0041_首帧视频.md","fields":[{"name":"ID","type":"STRING"},{"name":"<Picture 1>","type":"IMAGE"},{"name":"视频提示词","type":"TEXT"},{"name":"宽度","type":"INT"},{"name":"高度","type":"INT"},{"name":"视频秒数","type":"INT"}],"selected":{"id":"首帧视频-书房-深夜书房写作","values":{"ID":"首帧视频-书房-深夜书房写作","<Picture 1>":"@{场景推镜_书房玻璃窗}","视频提示词":"For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] The frame begins on a close-up of the study window glass, and <Picture 1> supplies the complete spatial information of the glass itself, the night outside the window and the interior of the study. At 0.00 seconds the focus rests on the glass surface, the reflections, water smudges and fine scratches on the glass are sharp, and the scene outside the window is out of focus.\nFrom 0.40 s to 2.20 s the focus moves smoothly from the glass surface toward the scene outside the window, the reflections and smudges on the glass turn into out-of-focus blur, and the night beyond, the window lights of distant buildings and the warm patches of the wet street lamps on the ground enter the sharp focal plane one after another, the focus shift proceeding evenly and continuously.\nFrom 2.20 s to 5.20 s the camera begins to pull back, the pull-back rate is slow and even, and the frame of the glass gradually expands toward both sides within the frame; a